ic data so every night he would  have one eye  as telescope observing observing the sky  and the other I would be writing these  figures down and running calculations  and night after night he split his  attention between the Stars and between  his figures and although he solved this  problem and did become famous he went  blind in one eye and ruined his his  sight in one of his eyes and I think  that just goes to show you kind of this  incredible focus and dedication and  intensity that many mathematicians have  had over time anyway Oilers number very  important more important than just  compound interest I'm gonna plot here  now one plus R this is how much you  would get back if you compounded once a  year and then e to the R if you  compounded continuously is always more e  to the R is always bigger than 1 plus R  and for small R it's not much better  remember we only got like 13 more sense  when R was 0.05 but when R is bigger  when R is 1 or 2 or 3 then this  compounded continuously gets better and  better and better faster okay so that's  really cool now you can also take this  discrete-time representation where my  money one year grows the next year and  the next year and the next year and you  can write this in continuous time as a  differential equation if you're getting  compounded continuously if your interest  is compounded continuously you can write  down this differential equation and so  what this says is that the rate of  change of my money every moment in time  is equal to R times X it's equal to my  rate times how much money I have in the  bank account now so the rate of change  of how much money I have is directly  proportional to how much money I have  and this totally makes sense this is  basically a statement of the rich get  richer faster the more money you have  the more money you make faster ok and  this simple linear differential equation  is the basis of kind of all of dynamical  systems and differential equations and  the solution is give